cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or workflow, please cite it as below.
  Please also cite the original studies for any isolates you use;
  they are listed in the Reference column of toxo-analysis/data/toxo_meta3.tsv.
title: "Toxoplasma gondii PCR-RFLP genotype database and Nextstrain build"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sachi
    family-names: Ramachandran
    affiliation: "University of Tennessee, Knoxville"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3973-9367"
  - given-names: Chunlei
    family-names: Su
    affiliation: "University of Tennessee, Knoxville"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8392-7108"
abstract: >-
  A public database of 1,662 Toxoplasma gondii isolates from 35 countries and
  35 host species, compiled from 53 published studies, with ToxoDB PCR-RFLP
  genotypes at 11 markers, host, location, collection year, MAT titer and mouse
  mortality. Each genotype is encoded as a 297 bp sequence of concatenated
  allele codes and analysed with a Nextstrain (Augur/Auspice) workflow to
  produce an interactive genotype-similarity tree and map. Code is licensed
  under MIT; data under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA).
keywords:
  - Toxoplasma gondii
  - PCR-RFLP
  - genotyping
  - molecular epidemiology
  - Nextstrain
  - zoonosis
